<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- dtrh-admission.md §1 integration consequence (WebView spike empirical): Avalonia's
     Win32 NativeControlHost requires supportedOS entries to create child windows
     (InvalidOperationException "Unable to create child window" without them). The embedded
     WebView2 surface needs this manifest. -->
<assembly manifestVersion="1.0" xmlns="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:asm.v1">
  <assemblyIdentity version="1.0.0.0" name="CcpClient.Desktop" />
  <!--
    DPI AWARENESS IS DECLARED HERE RATHER THAN INHERITED FROM A DEPENDENCY, and the values are the
    shipping product's own (ConditioningControlPanel/app.manifest:6-7: dpiAware true/pm +
    dpiAwareness PerMonitorV2). The port already RAN per-monitor-aware, but only because
    Avalonia.Win32 calls SetProcessDpiAwarenessContext when its platform initialises
    (Win32PlatformOptions.DpiAwareness, default PerMonitorDpiAware) - a default of a package, at
    phase 4, after this app's phases 1-3 and every pre-phase diagnostic have already run.

    WHAT THAT WINDOW COSTS, MEASURED ON THIS MACHINE (one display, 175%): an unmanifested net10
    apphost reads the primary monitor as 1646x1029 and a PER_MONITOR_AWARE_V2 one reads 2880x1800,
    which is the physical mode EnumDisplaySettings reports in both. Overlay/OverlayDisplays.cs and
    Effects/PrimaryDisplayPlacement.cs both document their rectangles as PHYSICAL pixels, and that
    is only true of a process that has said so. Nothing in phases 1-3 reads display geometry today;
    declaring it here means nothing added there ever has to know that.

    THIS DOES NOT FIGHT AVALONIA AND WAS CHECKED, NOT ASSUMED. With the manifest in force
    SetProcessDpiAwarenessContext returns FALSE with ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED (5) and the awareness stays
    PER_MONITOR_AWARE_V2 - the same value Avalonia was asking for, so its call becomes a no-op and
    nothing observable changes at runtime. The two declarations agree by construction; a
    disagreement would be a silent divergence in every coordinate this product computes.

    AND IT IS NOT A REPLACEMENT FOR AVALONIA'S CALL. A manifest only reaches the process when the
    apphost launches it: measured, `dotnet CcpClient.Desktop.dll` through the muxer runs UNAWARE
    (dotnet/runtime#13272) and is rescued by Avalonia at phase 4. Both mechanisms are load-bearing
    and neither is redundant.
  -->
  <application xmlns="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:asm.v3">
    <windowsSettings>
      <dpiAware xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/SMI/2005/WindowsSettings">true/pm</dpiAware>
      <dpiAwareness xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/SMI/2016/WindowsSettings">PerMonitorV2</dpiAwareness>
    </windowsSettings>
  </application>
  <compatibility xmlns="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:compatibility.v1">
    <application>
      <supportedOS Id="{8e0f7a12-bfb3-4fe8-b9a5-48fd50a15a9a}" /> <!-- Windows 10/11 -->
      <supportedOS Id="{1f676c76-80e1-4239-95bb-83d0f6d0da78}" /> <!-- Windows 8.1 -->
      <supportedOS Id="{4a2f28e3-53b9-4441-ba9c-d69d4a4a6e38}" /> <!-- Windows 8 -->
      <supportedOS Id="{35138b9a-5d96-4fbd-8e2d-a2440225f93a}" /> <!-- Windows 7 -->
    </application>
  </compatibility>
</assembly>
